# Copy to .env at the repo root and add your key. The example APIs (examples/demo_common/host.py)
# read this file, after the environment and the example's own .env; the SDK consoles and the
# MCP servers read the environment only. Never put a real key in this file.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Deploying an example API off loopback (e.g. the Osada Hygge vertical on Railway) ---
# The demo host answers only to localhost by default. When it runs behind a platform:
#   DEMO_ALLOWED_HOSTS   comma-separated Host names it will accept; "*" accepts any (the
#                        platform terminates TLS and, in a real deployment, fronts it with auth).
#   DEMO_ALLOWED_ORIGINS comma-separated exact browser origins allowed by CORS, e.g. the
#                        Vercel URL: https://your-app.vercel.app
#   SHOPPING_MODEL       overrides the shopping agent model id (default: claude-sonnet-4-6).
# DEMO_ALLOWED_HOSTS=*
# DEMO_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-app.vercel.app
#   DEMO_ALLOWED_ORIGIN_REGEX one pattern for a web app whose host changes on every
#     deploy; it must match the whole origin, so anchor it to hosts you own rather
#     than ending it in a bare provider domain.
# DEMO_ALLOWED_ORIGIN_REGEX=https://your-app-[a-z0-9]+-your-team\.vercel\.app
# SHOPPING_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6
